# Build context hygiene for the Glama-release bridge.
#
# The Dockerfile COPYs exactly one file (mcpb/server/index.js, twice), so almost
# nothing here reaches the image — but the CONTEXT is uploaded to the builder
# whole, and a context is a place secrets leak from even when the image is clean.
# Enforced by _hq/ops/container-check.mjs (R4 = this file exists, R5 = the secret
# patterns use the recursive form).

.git
.github
node_modules/
dist/
examples/
plugins/
alias/
bin/
mcpb/*.mcpb
*.md
!container/CONTAINER.md

# Secret patterns in the RECURSIVE form. A bare `.env` matches ONLY the context
# root, so nested copies (mcpb/server/.env.local) still ship — meshmarket proved
# that with a build canary. Never replace these with the bare form.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/id_rsa*
**/.claude-plugin/secrets*
